BT /F1 14 Tf 72 720 Td 20 TL (Chapter One) Tj T* () Tj T* (It was a bright cold day in April, and the clocks were striking thirteen.) Tj T* (The old house at the end of the street had been empty for many years.) Tj T* (Nobody remembered who had lived there, but everyone had a story about it.) Tj T* (Some said a sailor had built it with wood from his shipwrecked boat,) Tj T* (and others whispered that the garden was full of forgotten treasures.) Tj T* (Emma did not believe any of these stories, yet every morning on her way) Tj T* (to school she slowed down in front of the rusty gate and looked inside.) Tj T* ET
